Still reproduces on 4.4.0, and it does not need topology churn. Two instances, exactly_once_v2, num.standby.replicas=1, a two partition input, so each instance has one active and one standby task. One KafkaStreams#pause(), 60 s later KafkaStreams#resume(), and the state updater dies on the resume:

{noformat}
java.lang.IllegalStateException: The changelog reader is not restoring active tasks (is STANDBY_UPDATING) while trying to transit to update standby tasks: {...-store-changelog-1=RESTORING STANDBY (currentOffset 2133, endOffset null)}
    at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StoreChangelogReader.transitToUpdateStandby(StoreChangelogReader.java:333)
    at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.DefaultStateUpdater$StateUpdaterThread.resumeTask(DefaultStateUpdater.java:744)
    at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.DefaultStateUpdater$StateUpdaterThread.resumeTasks(DefaultStateUpdater.java:263)
    at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.DefaultStateUpdater$StateUpdaterThread.runOnce(DefaultStateUpdater.java:215)
    at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.DefaultStateUpdater$StateUpdaterThread.run(DefaultStateUpdater.java:170)
{noformat}

The stream thread then fails with "The state updater died and cannot update tasks anymore" and the client goes RUNNING -> PENDING_ERROR -> ERROR. The resumeTask call is unchanged on trunk (DefaultStateUpdater 751-752). PR #22864 replaces it with the guarded maybeTransitionChangelogReader(), so it covers this path.

The fix would be something like this:
{code:java}
    public Optional<Node> getPartitionLeaderEndpoint(String topicName, int partitionId, ListenerName listenerName) {
        MetadataImage image = currentImage;
        return Optional.ofNullable(image.topics().getTopic(topicName))
            .flatMap(topic -> Optional.ofNullable(topic.partitions().get(partitionId)))
            .flatMap(partition -> {
                // If partition is found we must return non-empty optional.
                BrokerRegistration broker = image.cluster().broker(partition.leader);
                Node node = (broker == null)
                        ? Node.noNode()
                        : broker.node(listenerName.value()).orElse(Node.noNode());
                return Optional.of(node);
            });
    } {code}

